diff --git a/src/apu/README.md b/src/apu/README.md
index cc0925e..4a9a089 100644
--- a/src/apu/README.md
+++ b/src/apu/README.md
@@ -19,10 +19,14 @@ clean checkout and make the Rust 1.99 toolchain available to CMake.
 
 The GP and EP RAM windows are routed through the APU MMIO handler, including
 the GP mixbuffer alias and 24-bit word masking. P-memory writes use the FFI
-write API when that engine is enabled so translated code is invalidated. The
-reset register is stored and reset assertion resets the core; reset release
-does not yet load firmware. Scratch bootstrap, cycle scheduling, peripheral
-callbacks, FIFO/DMA, and DSP audio remain unimplemented. The optional FFI core
+write API when that engine is enabled so translated code is invalidated. Reset
+release now copies 0x800 words from the guest scratch scatter/gather table into
+P memory through the runtime's bounded physical-memory resolver. A focused
+synthetic test verifies page-boundary copies, 24-bit masking, and rejection of
+an incomplete descriptor table. One bounded Steel Battalion startup with the
+optional FFI enabled logged successful GP and EP bootstraps; it did not execute
+the DSP programs or verify audible output. Cycle scheduling, peripheral
+callbacks, FIFO/DMA, and DSP audio remain incomplete. The optional FFI core
 stays off by default, and this is not playable-audio support.
 
